    "https://www.stmarytx.edu/about/jobs/": {
      "title": "University Closed",
      "description": "HR - Job Openings at St. Mary's University St. Mary's University 1 Camino Santa Maria San Antonio , TX 78228 +1-210-436-3011 https://www.stmarytx.edu William Joseph Chaminade Skip to main content University Closed In observance of Labor Day on Monday, Sept. 7 , all St. Mary’s University offices will be closed and classes canceled. Offices will reopen and classes will resume on Tuesday, Sept. 8. Resources For: Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parent & Family Apply Visit Request Info Give Now About Events Calendar History Leadership Map Mission Rankings Academics Career Center Centers and Institutes Degrees and Programs Faculty Registrar Research Schools Student Success Admission Apply for Admission Cost and Aid Graduate Military Orientation Tuition and Fees Visit Campus Athletics Campus Life Student Housing and Amenities Spiritual Life Student Life Student Services Center for International Programs Outreach Camps Counseling Service STEM Outreach  Search  Submit Human Resources Jobs Home » About St. Mary’s » Human Resources Jobs In this Section About St. Mary’s Calendar Hispanic-Serving Institution History of St. Mary’s University Honors and Rankings Human Resources Jobs Inclusive Excellence Laudato Si’ Leadership Board of Trustees Office of the Provost President President’s Ambassadors Presidents and Deans Emeriti Professors Emeriti Mission and Vision Notable Alumni Ombuds Presidential Award Recipients Saint John’s Bible at St. Mary’s Signature Events Commencement Commencement Ceremony Program Commencement Speaker Family Weekend Livestream Speakers and Lectures St. Mary’s University 5K for the Neighborhood Social Media The College Tour Series The Rattler Ring Traditions Why St. Mary’s St. Mary’s Job Openings View All Current Job Postings School of Law Dean Leadership Profile School of Science, Engineering and Technology Dean Leadership Profile College of Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Dean Leadership Profile St. Mary’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants requiring assistance with the online application should contact the Texas Workforce Commission. Paper applications are accepted in person. Looking for Student Employment or Graduate Assistantships? View current opportunities. Regarding H-1B VISA Sponsorship Please note that St. Mary’s University is currently unable to offer H-1B sponsorship for employment. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship. About St. Mary’s University Founded in 1852 by the Society of Mary, St. Mary’s University is a comprehensive Catholic and Marianist university with a strong tradition of integrating liberal arts with professional studies. St. Mary’s serves a diverse student population enrolled in graduate and undergraduate programs within our four schools: Humanities and Social Sciences; Greehey School of Business; Science, Engineering and Technology; and Law. St. Mary’s has been cited as a national model for high graduation rates among Texas colleges and is ranked among the best in the West Region for value and academic quality by U.S. News & World Report . Undergraduate research, community service, internships and study abroad are some of the opportunities that enhance the St. Mary’s experience. St. Mary’s has about 200 full-time faculty members, 94 percent with terminal degrees. The University offers degrees in more than 40 academic programs, including pre-professional programs in medicine, nursing, dentistry, pharmacy, allied health, and law. St. Mary’s is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution, the oldest Catholic university in the Southwest and a steadfast advocate of the Marianist mission of academic excellence and servant leadership. To all applicants – Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report St. Mary’s University is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at www.stmarytx.edu/compliance/clery-act-information/ . If you would like a hard copy of the report, stop by the St. Mary’s Police Department Office at One Camino Santa Maria, San Antonio, Texas 78228 or request a copy be mailed to you by calling 210-436-3330. The report contains information, as required by law, regarding campus security and personal safety. The report also contains information about fire statistics in campus residential facilities and crime statistics for the three previous calendar years that occurred on campus; property owned or controlled by the University; and public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. Contact Us Human Resources St. Louis Hall, Room 012 St. Mary’s University One Camino Santa Maria San Antonio, Texas 78228 Phone: 210-436-3725 Fax: 210-431-2223 humanresources@stmarytx.edu Office Hours: 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. Back to top Request Info Visit Apply Give Now Compliance Directory Gateway HR Jobs Police Policies Privacy Reporting Webmail St. Mary’s University Websites Campus Map Nondiscrimination / Title IX Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information List of social media accounts © 2026 All rights reserved. Contact 210-436-3011 One Camino Santa Maria, San Antonio, TX 78228. We use cookies to collect and analyze information on site performance and usage, and to enhance and customize content and targeted advertisements. Accept Cookies Reject Cookies Cookie Policy You can revoke your consent any time using the Cookie Notice button. Cookie Notice"
